{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../examples/aggregation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Aggregation"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Aggregation is independent from column grouping. Register "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowAggregationFeature"},{"type":"text","value":"\nwhenever columns calculate totals or aggregated values. Add\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnGroupingFeature"},{"type":"text","value":" separately only when the table also groups rows."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"aggregation-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Aggregation Setup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Register only the built-in functions referenced by name. Passing a definition\ndirectly to a column does not require a registry entry."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  rowAggregationFeature,\n  aggregationFn_count,\n  aggregationFn_extent,\n  aggregationFn_mean,\n  aggregationFn_sum,\n  tableFeatures,\n  constructTable,\n} from '@tanstack/table-core'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowAggregationFeature,\n  aggregationFns: {\n    count: aggregationFn_count,\n    extent: aggregationFn_extent,\n    mean: aggregationFn_mean,\n    sum: aggregationFn_sum,\n  },\n})\n\nconst table = constructTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The aggregation feature does not require a grouped row model. This makes grand\ntotals and custom row-subset totals available in otherwise ordinary tables."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The full "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregationFns"},{"type":"text","value":" registry remains available for compatibility, but it\nbundles every built-in. Tables using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stockFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" already include\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowAggregationFeature"},{"type":"text","value":"; they still need the definitions that named column\noptions should resolve to."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"column-aggregations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Aggregations"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A column accepts one aggregation or an array. A single entry returns a scalar;\nmultiple entries return an object keyed by the aggregation name or descriptor\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"columnHelper.accessor('amount', {\n  aggregationFn: 'sum',\n})\n\ncolumnHelper.accessor('score', {\n  aggregationFn: ['count', 'mean', { id: 'range', aggregationFn: 'extent' }],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"String values remain backward-compatible. Use descriptors when a result needs\na stable custom key or options."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A scalar "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregationFn"},{"type":"text","value":" can be a registered name, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'auto'"},{"type":"text","value":", or an inline\ndefinition. Every entry in an aggregation array needs a unique stable id.\nDuplicate ids, missing descriptor ids, and unregistered names warn in\ndevelopment and preserve the affected key with an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":" value."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Multiple aggregations can be read with a typed result:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const scoreColumn = columnHelper.accessor('score', {\n  aggregationFn: ['count', 'mean', { id: 'range', aggregationFn: 'extent' }],\n  footer: ({ column }) => {\n    const result = column.getAggregationValue<{\n      count: number\n      mean: number | undefined\n      range: [number | undefined, number | undefined]\n    }>()\n\n    return `${result.count} values; mean ${result.mean}; range ${result.range}`\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"grand-totals-and-row-subsets","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grand Totals and Row Subsets"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getAggregationValue()"},{"type":"text","value":" without arguments to aggregate the default\npre-grouped row model. Filtering is included; grouping, sorting, expansion, and\npagination do not change that default total."}]},{"type":"code","value":"footer: ({ column }) => column.getAggregationValue<number>().toLocaleString()","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass one options object with rows from any row model to choose a different set:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"column.getAggregationValue({ rows: table.getCoreRowModel().rows })\ncolumn.getAggregationValue({ rows: table.getRowModel().rows })\ncolumn.getAggregationValue({ rows: table.getFilteredSelectedRowModel().rows })\ncolumn.getAggregationValue({ rows: table.getCoreRowModel().rows.slice(0, 3) })\ncolumn.getAggregationValue({ rows: table.getCoreRowModel().rows, maxDepth: 1 })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Depth is relative to the supplied row array. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":" selects those roots, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1"},{"type":"text","value":"\nselects their direct sub-rows, and so on. Selection returns a unique frontier:\na branch that ends before the maximum depth contributes its deepest available\nrow. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Infinity"},{"type":"text","value":" selects terminal rows."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configure "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxAggregationDepth"},{"type":"text","value":" on the column for cached default calls (it\ndefaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":"), or pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxDepth"},{"type":"text","value":" in the options object as an explicit\noverride. Every aggregation configured on the column receives the same\nselected rows. Explicit row calls are recomputed each time; the default call is\ncached against its row model, depth, registry, and column aggregation option."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getMaxSubRowDepth()"},{"type":"text","value":" returns the deepest structural depth in the core\nrow model. To stop one level before the deepest sub-row frontier:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const maxDepth = Math.max(0, table.getMaxSubRowDepth() - 1)\ncolumn.getAggregationValue({\n  rows: table.getCoreRowModel().rows,\n  maxDepth,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"grouped-aggregation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grouped Aggregation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grouped aggregation composes two independent features. Register both, add the\ngrouped row-model slot, and configure aggregation functions on the columns that\nshould produce grouped values."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const features = tableFeatures({\n  rowAggregationFeature,\n  columnGroupingFeature,\n  groupedRowModel: createGroupedRowModel(),\n  aggregationFns: { sum: aggregationFn_sum },\n})\n\ncolumnHelper.accessor('visits', {\n  aggregationFn: 'sum',\n  aggregatedCell: ({ getValue }) => getValue<number>().toLocaleString(),\n  footer: ({ column }) => column.getAggregationValue<number>().toLocaleString(),\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregatedCell"},{"type":"text","value":" column option renders aggregate values on synthetic\ngrouped rows. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell.getIsAggregated()"},{"type":"text","value":" to identify a grouped aggregate\ncell. Footer rendering uses the adapter's normal footer renderer. Grouping-only\ntables do not expose "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell.getIsAggregated()"},{"type":"text","value":"; it belongs to\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rowAggregationFeature"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"custom-aggregation-definitions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom Aggregation Definitions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom aggregations are context-based definitions. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rows"},{"type":"text","value":" contains the unique\nfrontier selected at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxDepth"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getValue(row)"},{"type":"text","value":" reads the current column's\nvalue."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const joined = constructAggregationFn<any, any, string, string>({\n  aggregate: ({ rows, getValue }) =>\n    rows\n      .map((row) => getValue(row))\n      .filter(Boolean)\n      .join(', '),\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The context also includes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnId"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxDepth"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table"},{"type":"text","value":". During\ngrouped aggregation it includes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"groupingRow"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subRows"},{"type":"text","value":"; root and\ncaller-supplied-row aggregation omit those properties. The grouping depth is\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"groupingRow.depth"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subRows"},{"type":"text","value":" contains the immediate rows at that grouping\nlevel, so an aggregation can explicitly choose immediate sub-rows instead of\nthe depth-selected "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rows"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const subRowCount = constructAggregationFn<any, any, unknown, number>({\n  aggregate: ({ subRows, rows }) => (subRows ?? rows).length,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"At the terminal grouping level, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subRows"},{"type":"text","value":" contains direct data rows. At a\nnested level, it contains the immediate synthetic sub-row groups. All built-in\naggregation definitions consume the same depth-selected "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rows"},{"type":"text","value":"; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subRows"},{"type":"text","value":"\nremains available when a custom definition intentionally needs the grouping\nrow's immediate structural children."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a result that can be combined more efficiently from already-computed\nsub-row results, provide a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"merge"},{"type":"text","value":" function:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const sum = constructAggregationFn<any, any, unknown, number>({\n  aggregate: ({ rows, getValue }) =>\n    rows.reduce((total, row) => {\n      const value = getValue(row)\n      return total + (typeof value === 'number' ? value : 0)\n    }, 0),\n  merge: ({ subRowResults }) =>\n    subRowResults.reduce((total, value) => total + value, 0),\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"merge"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subRowResults[i]"},{"type":"text","value":" is the aggregation result previously computed\nfor "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subRows[i]"},{"type":"text","value":". Without "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"merge"},{"type":"text","value":", nested grouping calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregate"},{"type":"text","value":" with both\nthe group's depth-selected "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rows"},{"type":"text","value":" and its immediate "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subRows"},{"type":"text","value":". This\ncontext-based form replaces the previous callable aggregation signature and its\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fromRows"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resolveDataValue"},{"type":"text","value":" properties while preserving access to both\nrow sets."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"providing-server-or-external-values","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Providing Server or External Values"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A column can handle aggregation-value requests before local calculation:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const amountColumn = columnHelper.accessor('amount', {\n  aggregationFn: 'sum',\n  getAggregationValue: ({ rows }) => {\n    if (rows !== undefined) return undefined // use local fallback for overrides\n    return { value: serverTotals.amount }\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returning "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ value }"},{"type":"text","value":" marks the request as handled, including\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ value: undefined }"},{"type":"text","value":". Returning "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":" uses the local fallback. Put the\nsame provider on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultColumn"},{"type":"text","value":" to share it across columns."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"manualAggregation: true"},{"type":"text","value":" to disable the local fallback for\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getAggregationValue()"},{"type":"text","value":". This is separate from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"manualGrouping"},{"type":"text","value":", which\ncontrols whether the grouped row model runs. See the\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../../../guide/client-side-vs-server-side","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client-Side vs Server-Side Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nfor guidance on choosing where the full data pipeline should run."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"built-in-definitions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Built-in Definitions"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sum"},{"type":"text","value":": sums numeric values; non-numbers contribute zero."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"count"},{"type":"text","value":": counts rows."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"min"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"max"},{"type":"text","value":": find numeric or Date bounds."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"extent"},{"type":"text","value":": returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[min, max]"},{"type":"text","value":"; an empty input returns\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[undefined, undefined]"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mean"},{"type":"text","value":": averages numeric and number-like non-null values."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"median"},{"type":"text","value":": requires every row value to be a number."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unique"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"uniqueCount"},{"type":"text","value":": use JavaScript "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Set"},{"type":"text","value":" semantics."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"first"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"last"},{"type":"text","value":": return the positional value, including a nullish value."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregationFn: 'auto'"},{"type":"text","value":" inspects the first core row value. Numbers resolve to a\nregistered "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sum"},{"type":"text","value":", Dates resolve to a registered "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"extent"},{"type":"text","value":", and other values do\nnot resolve an aggregation."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"web-workers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Web Workers"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Worker-backed grouped row models eagerly compute explicitly configured grouped\naggregates in the worker. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getAggregationValue()"},{"type":"text","value":" still executes its\nfinal total on the main thread over the selected row model. Aggregation results\ncrossing the worker boundary must be structured-cloneable. See the\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../../../guide/worker-row-models","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Worker Row Models Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for setup and\nlimitations."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2},{"id":"aggregation-setup","text":"Aggregation Setup","level":2},{"id":"column-aggregations","text":"Column Aggregations","level":2},{"id":"grand-totals-and-row-subsets","text":"Grand Totals and Row Subsets","level":2},{"id":"grouped-aggregation","text":"Grouped Aggregation","level":2},{"id":"custom-aggregation-definitions","text":"Custom Aggregation Definitions","level":2},{"id":"providing-server-or-external-values","text":"Providing Server or External Values","level":2},{"id":"built-in-definitions","text":"Built-in Definitions","level":2},{"id":"web-workers","text":"Web Workers","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n## Examples\n\n- [Aggregation](../examples/aggregation)\n\nAggregation is independent from column grouping. Register `rowAggregationFeature`\nwhenever columns calculate totals or aggregated values. Add\n`columnGroupingFeature` separately only when the table also groups rows.\n\n## Aggregation Setup\n\nRegister only the built-in functions referenced by name. Passing a definition\ndirectly to a column does not require a registry entry.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  rowAggregationFeature,\n  aggregationFn_count,\n  aggregationFn_extent,\n  aggregationFn_mean,\n  aggregationFn_sum,\n  tableFeatures,\n  constructTable,\n} from '@tanstack/table-core'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowAggregationFeature,\n  aggregationFns: {\n    count: aggregationFn_count,\n    extent: aggregationFn_extent,\n    mean: aggregationFn_mean,\n    sum: aggregationFn_sum,\n  },\n})\n\nconst table = constructTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data,\n})\n```\n\nThe aggregation feature does not require a grouped row model. This makes grand\ntotals and custom row-subset totals available in otherwise ordinary tables.\n\nThe full `aggregationFns` registry remains available for compatibility, but it\nbundles every built-in. Tables using `stockFeatures` already include\n`rowAggregationFeature`; they still need the definitions that named column\noptions should resolve to.\n\n## Column Aggregations\n\nA column accepts one aggregation or an array. A single entry returns a scalar;\nmultiple entries return an object keyed by the aggregation name or descriptor\n`id`.\n\n```ts\ncolumnHelper.accessor('amount', {\n  aggregationFn: 'sum',\n})\n\ncolumnHelper.accessor('score', {\n  aggregationFn: ['count', 'mean', { id: 'range', aggregationFn: 'extent' }],\n})\n```\n\nString values remain backward-compatible. Use descriptors when a result needs\na stable custom key or options.\n\nA scalar `aggregationFn` can be a registered name, `'auto'`, or an inline\ndefinition. Every entry in an aggregation array needs a unique stable id.\nDuplicate ids, missing descriptor ids, and unregistered names warn in\ndevelopment and preserve the affected key with an `undefined` value.\n\nMultiple aggregations can be read with a typed result:\n\n```ts\nconst scoreColumn = columnHelper.accessor('score', {\n  aggregationFn: ['count', 'mean', { id: 'range', aggregationFn: 'extent' }],\n  footer: ({ column }) => {\n    const result = column.getAggregationValue<{\n      count: number\n      mean: number | undefined\n      range: [number | undefined, number | undefined]\n    }>()\n\n    return `${result.count} values; mean ${result.mean}; range ${result.range}`\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Grand Totals and Row Subsets\n\nCall `column.getAggregationValue()` without arguments to aggregate the default\npre-grouped row model. Filtering is included; grouping, sorting, expansion, and\npagination do not change that default total.\n\n```ts\nfooter: ({ column }) => column.getAggregationValue<number>().toLocaleString()\n```\n\nPass one options object with rows from any row model to choose a different set:\n\n```ts\ncolumn.getAggregationValue({ rows: table.getCoreRowModel().rows })\ncolumn.getAggregationValue({ rows: table.getRowModel().rows })\ncolumn.getAggregationValue({ rows: table.getFilteredSelectedRowModel().rows })\ncolumn.getAggregationValue({ rows: table.getCoreRowModel().rows.slice(0, 3) })\ncolumn.getAggregationValue({ rows: table.getCoreRowModel().rows, maxDepth: 1 })\n```\n\nDepth is relative to the supplied row array. `0` selects those roots, `1`\nselects their direct sub-rows, and so on. Selection returns a unique frontier:\na branch that ends before the maximum depth contributes its deepest available\nrow. `Infinity` selects terminal rows.\n\nConfigure `maxAggregationDepth` on the column for cached default calls (it\ndefaults to `0`), or pass `maxDepth` in the options object as an explicit\noverride. Every aggregation configured on the column receives the same\nselected rows. Explicit row calls are recomputed each time; the default call is\ncached against its row model, depth, registry, and column aggregation option.\n\n`table.getMaxSubRowDepth()` returns the deepest structural depth in the core\nrow model. To stop one level before the deepest sub-row frontier:\n\n```ts\nconst maxDepth = Math.max(0, table.getMaxSubRowDepth() - 1)\ncolumn.getAggregationValue({\n  rows: table.getCoreRowModel().rows,\n  maxDepth,\n})\n```\n\n## Grouped Aggregation\n\nGrouped aggregation composes two independent features. Register both, add the\ngrouped row-model slot, and configure aggregation functions on the columns that\nshould produce grouped values.\n\n```ts\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowAggregationFeature,\n  columnGroupingFeature,\n  groupedRowModel: createGroupedRowModel(),\n  aggregationFns: { sum: aggregationFn_sum },\n})\n\ncolumnHelper.accessor('visits', {\n  aggregationFn: 'sum',\n  aggregatedCell: ({ getValue }) => getValue<number>().toLocaleString(),\n  footer: ({ column }) => column.getAggregationValue<number>().toLocaleString(),\n})\n```\n\nThe `aggregatedCell` column option renders aggregate values on synthetic\ngrouped rows. Use `cell.getIsAggregated()` to identify a grouped aggregate\ncell. Footer rendering uses the adapter's normal footer renderer. Grouping-only\ntables do not expose `cell.getIsAggregated()`; it belongs to\n`rowAggregationFeature`.\n\n## Custom Aggregation Definitions\n\nCustom aggregations are context-based definitions. `rows` contains the unique\nfrontier selected at `maxDepth`, and `getValue(row)` reads the current column's\nvalue.\n\n```ts\nconst joined = constructAggregationFn<any, any, string, string>({\n  aggregate: ({ rows, getValue }) =>\n    rows\n      .map((row) => getValue(row))\n      .filter(Boolean)\n      .join(', '),\n})\n```\n\nThe context also includes `column`, `columnId`, `maxDepth`, and `table`. During\ngrouped aggregation it includes `groupingRow` and `subRows`; root and\ncaller-supplied-row aggregation omit those properties. The grouping depth is\n`groupingRow.depth`. `subRows` contains the immediate rows at that grouping\nlevel, so an aggregation can explicitly choose immediate sub-rows instead of\nthe depth-selected `rows`:\n\n```ts\nconst subRowCount = constructAggregationFn<any, any, unknown, number>({\n  aggregate: ({ subRows, rows }) => (subRows ?? rows).length,\n})\n```\n\nAt the terminal grouping level, `subRows` contains direct data rows. At a\nnested level, it contains the immediate synthetic sub-row groups. All built-in\naggregation definitions consume the same depth-selected `rows`; `subRows`\nremains available when a custom definition intentionally needs the grouping\nrow's immediate structural children.\n\nFor a result that can be combined more efficiently from already-computed\nsub-row results, provide a `merge` function:\n\n```ts\nconst sum = constructAggregationFn<any, any, unknown, number>({\n  aggregate: ({ rows, getValue }) =>\n    rows.reduce((total, row) => {\n      const value = getValue(row)\n      return total + (typeof value === 'number' ? value : 0)\n    }, 0),\n  merge: ({ subRowResults }) =>\n    subRowResults.reduce((total, value) => total + value, 0),\n})\n```\n\nFor `merge`, `subRowResults[i]` is the aggregation result previously computed\nfor `subRows[i]`. Without `merge`, nested grouping calls `aggregate` with both\nthe group's depth-selected `rows` and its immediate `subRows`. This\ncontext-based form replaces the previous callable aggregation signature and its\n`fromRows` and `resolveDataValue` properties while preserving access to both\nrow sets.\n\n## Providing Server or External Values\n\nA column can handle aggregation-value requests before local calculation:\n\n```ts\nconst amountColumn = columnHelper.accessor('amount', {\n  aggregationFn: 'sum',\n  getAggregationValue: ({ rows }) => {\n    if (rows !== undefined) return undefined // use local fallback for overrides\n    return { value: serverTotals.amount }\n  },\n})\n```\n\nReturning `{ value }` marks the request as handled, including\n`{ value: undefined }`. Returning `undefined` uses the local fallback. Put the\nsame provider on `defaultColumn` to share it across columns.\n\nSet `manualAggregation: true` to disable the local fallback for\n`column.getAggregationValue()`. This is separate from `manualGrouping`, which\ncontrols whether the grouped row model runs. See the\n[Client-Side vs Server-Side Guide](../../../guide/client-side-vs-server-side)\nfor guidance on choosing where the full data pipeline should run.\n\n## Built-in Definitions\n\n- `sum`: sums numeric values; non-numbers contribute zero.\n- `count`: counts rows.\n- `min` / `max`: find numeric or Date bounds.\n- `extent`: returns `[min, max]`; an empty input returns\n  `[undefined, undefined]`.\n- `mean`: averages numeric and number-like non-null values.\n- `median`: requires every row value to be a number.\n- `unique` / `uniqueCount`: use JavaScript `Set` semantics.\n- `first` / `last`: return the positional value, including a nullish value.\n\n`aggregationFn: 'auto'` inspects the first core row value. Numbers resolve to a\nregistered `sum`, Dates resolve to a registered `extent`, and other values do\nnot resolve an aggregation.\n\n## Web Workers\n\nWorker-backed grouped row models eagerly compute explicitly configured grouped\naggregates in the worker. `column.getAggregationValue()` still executes its\nfinal total on the main thread over the selected row model. Aggregation results\ncrossing the worker boundary must be structured-cloneable. See the\n[Worker Row Models Guide](../../../guide/worker-row-models) for setup and\nlimitations.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Aggregation (Vanilla) Guide\n---\n\n## Examples\n\n- [Aggregation](../examples/aggregation)\n\nAggregation is independent from column grouping. Register `rowAggregationFeature`\nwhenever columns calculate totals or aggregated values. Add\n`columnGroupingFeature` separately only when the table also groups rows.\n\n## Aggregation Setup\n\nRegister only the built-in functions referenced by name. Passing a definition\ndirectly to a column does not require a registry entry.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  rowAggregationFeature,\n  aggregationFn_count,\n  aggregationFn_extent,\n  aggregationFn_mean,\n  aggregationFn_sum,\n  tableFeatures,\n  constructTable,\n} from '@tanstack/table-core'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowAggregationFeature,\n  aggregationFns: {\n    count: aggregationFn_count,\n    extent: aggregationFn_extent,\n    mean: aggregationFn_mean,\n    sum: aggregationFn_sum,\n  },\n})\n\nconst table = constructTable({\n  features,\n  columns,\n  data,\n})\n```\n\nThe aggregation feature does not require a grouped row model. This makes grand\ntotals and custom row-subset totals available in otherwise ordinary tables.\n\nThe full `aggregationFns` registry remains available for compatibility, but it\nbundles every built-in. Tables using `stockFeatures` already include\n`rowAggregationFeature`; they still need the definitions that named column\noptions should resolve to.\n\n## Column Aggregations\n\nA column accepts one aggregation or an array. A single entry returns a scalar;\nmultiple entries return an object keyed by the aggregation name or descriptor\n`id`.\n\n```ts\ncolumnHelper.accessor('amount', {\n  aggregationFn: 'sum',\n})\n\ncolumnHelper.accessor('score', {\n  aggregationFn: ['count', 'mean', { id: 'range', aggregationFn: 'extent' }],\n})\n```\n\nString values remain backward-compatible. Use descriptors when a result needs\na stable custom key or options.\n\nA scalar `aggregationFn` can be a registered name, `'auto'`, or an inline\ndefinition. Every entry in an aggregation array needs a unique stable id.\nDuplicate ids, missing descriptor ids, and unregistered names warn in\ndevelopment and preserve the affected key with an `undefined` value.\n\nMultiple aggregations can be read with a typed result:\n\n```ts\nconst scoreColumn = columnHelper.accessor('score', {\n  aggregationFn: ['count', 'mean', { id: 'range', aggregationFn: 'extent' }],\n  footer: ({ column }) => {\n    const result = column.getAggregationValue<{\n      count: number\n      mean: number | undefined\n      range: [number | undefined, number | undefined]\n    }>()\n\n    return `${result.count} values; mean ${result.mean}; range ${result.range}`\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Grand Totals and Row Subsets\n\nCall `column.getAggregationValue()` without arguments to aggregate the default\npre-grouped row model. Filtering is included; grouping, sorting, expansion, and\npagination do not change that default total.\n\n```ts\nfooter: ({ column }) => column.getAggregationValue<number>().toLocaleString()\n```\n\nPass one options object with rows from any row model to choose a different set:\n\n```ts\ncolumn.getAggregationValue({ rows: table.getCoreRowModel().rows })\ncolumn.getAggregationValue({ rows: table.getRowModel().rows })\ncolumn.getAggregationValue({ rows: table.getFilteredSelectedRowModel().rows })\ncolumn.getAggregationValue({ rows: table.getCoreRowModel().rows.slice(0, 3) })\ncolumn.getAggregationValue({ rows: table.getCoreRowModel().rows, maxDepth: 1 })\n```\n\nDepth is relative to the supplied row array. `0` selects those roots, `1`\nselects their direct sub-rows, and so on. Selection returns a unique frontier:\na branch that ends before the maximum depth contributes its deepest available\nrow. `Infinity` selects terminal rows.\n\nConfigure `maxAggregationDepth` on the column for cached default calls (it\ndefaults to `0`), or pass `maxDepth` in the options object as an explicit\noverride. Every aggregation configured on the column receives the same\nselected rows. Explicit row calls are recomputed each time; the default call is\ncached against its row model, depth, registry, and column aggregation option.\n\n`table.getMaxSubRowDepth()` returns the deepest structural depth in the core\nrow model. To stop one level before the deepest sub-row frontier:\n\n```ts\nconst maxDepth = Math.max(0, table.getMaxSubRowDepth() - 1)\ncolumn.getAggregationValue({\n  rows: table.getCoreRowModel().rows,\n  maxDepth,\n})\n```\n\n## Grouped Aggregation\n\nGrouped aggregation composes two independent features. Register both, add the\ngrouped row-model slot, and configure aggregation functions on the columns that\nshould produce grouped values.\n\n```ts\nconst features = tableFeatures({\n  rowAggregationFeature,\n  columnGroupingFeature,\n  groupedRowModel: createGroupedRowModel(),\n  aggregationFns: { sum: aggregationFn_sum },\n})\n\ncolumnHelper.accessor('visits', {\n  aggregationFn: 'sum',\n  aggregatedCell: ({ getValue }) => getValue<number>().toLocaleString(),\n  footer: ({ column }) => column.getAggregationValue<number>().toLocaleString(),\n})\n```\n\nThe `aggregatedCell` column option renders aggregate values on synthetic\ngrouped rows. Use `cell.getIsAggregated()` to identify a grouped aggregate\ncell. Footer rendering uses the adapter's normal footer renderer. Grouping-only\ntables do not expose `cell.getIsAggregated()`; it belongs to\n`rowAggregationFeature`.\n\n## Custom Aggregation Definitions\n\nCustom aggregations are context-based definitions. `rows` contains the unique\nfrontier selected at `maxDepth`, and `getValue(row)` reads the current column's\nvalue.\n\n```ts\nconst joined = constructAggregationFn<any, any, string, string>({\n  aggregate: ({ rows, getValue }) =>\n    rows\n      .map((row) => getValue(row))\n      .filter(Boolean)\n      .join(', '),\n})\n```\n\nThe context also includes `column`, `columnId`, `maxDepth`, and `table`. During\ngrouped aggregation it includes `groupingRow` and `subRows`; root and\ncaller-supplied-row aggregation omit those properties. The grouping depth is\n`groupingRow.depth`. `subRows` contains the immediate rows at that grouping\nlevel, so an aggregation can explicitly choose immediate sub-rows instead of\nthe depth-selected `rows`:\n\n```ts\nconst subRowCount = constructAggregationFn<any, any, unknown, number>({\n  aggregate: ({ subRows, rows }) => (subRows ?? rows).length,\n})\n```\n\nAt the terminal grouping level, `subRows` contains direct data rows. At a\nnested level, it contains the immediate synthetic sub-row groups. All built-in\naggregation definitions consume the same depth-selected `rows`; `subRows`\nremains available when a custom definition intentionally needs the grouping\nrow's immediate structural children.\n\nFor a result that can be combined more efficiently from already-computed\nsub-row results, provide a `merge` function:\n\n```ts\nconst sum = constructAggregationFn<any, any, unknown, number>({\n  aggregate: ({ rows, getValue }) =>\n    rows.reduce((total, row) => {\n      const value = getValue(row)\n      return total + (typeof value === 'number' ? value : 0)\n    }, 0),\n  merge: ({ subRowResults }) =>\n    subRowResults.reduce((total, value) => total + value, 0),\n})\n```\n\nFor `merge`, `subRowResults[i]` is the aggregation result previously computed\nfor `subRows[i]`. Without `merge`, nested grouping calls `aggregate` with both\nthe group's depth-selected `rows` and its immediate `subRows`. This\ncontext-based form replaces the previous callable aggregation signature and its\n`fromRows` and `resolveDataValue` properties while preserving access to both\nrow sets.\n\n## Providing Server or External Values\n\nA column can handle aggregation-value requests before local calculation:\n\n```ts\nconst amountColumn = columnHelper.accessor('amount', {\n  aggregationFn: 'sum',\n  getAggregationValue: ({ rows }) => {\n    if (rows !== undefined) return undefined // use local fallback for overrides\n    return { value: serverTotals.amount }\n  },\n})\n```\n\nReturning `{ value }` marks the request as handled, including\n`{ value: undefined }`. Returning `undefined` uses the local fallback. Put the\nsame provider on `defaultColumn` to share it across columns.\n\nSet `manualAggregation: true` to disable the local fallback for\n`column.getAggregationValue()`. This is separate from `manualGrouping`, which\ncontrols whether the grouped row model runs. See the\n[Client-Side vs Server-Side Guide](../../../guide/client-side-vs-server-side)\nfor guidance on choosing where the full data pipeline should run.\n\n## Built-in Definitions\n\n- `sum`: sums numeric values; non-numbers contribute zero.\n- `count`: counts rows.\n- `min` / `max`: find numeric or Date bounds.\n- `extent`: returns `[min, max]`; an empty input returns\n  `[undefined, undefined]`.\n- `mean`: averages numeric and number-like non-null values.\n- `median`: requires every row value to be a number.\n- `unique` / `uniqueCount`: use JavaScript `Set` semantics.\n- `first` / `last`: return the positional value, including a nullish value.\n\n`aggregationFn: 'auto'` inspects the first core row value. Numbers resolve to a\nregistered `sum`, Dates resolve to a registered `extent`, and other values do\nnot resolve an aggregation.\n\n## Web Workers\n\nWorker-backed grouped row models eagerly compute explicitly configured grouped\naggregates in the worker. `column.getAggregationValue()` still executes its\nfinal total on the main thread over the selected row model. Aggregation results\ncrossing the worker boundary must be structured-cloneable. See the\n[Worker Row Models Guide](../../../guide/worker-row-models) for setup and\nlimitations.\n"}
